--context

Check out the @comm-context for general background of the archival metadata project, where the
data-carousel-AM package is meant to collect the recall history, along with all the metadata,
and the arcmeta package consists of scripts used to analyze the data, calculate entropy of metadata
fields etc.

--task A: there is the @data-carousel-AM/data/prodsyslogs.csv file with recall history info,
create a script that will do the following:
1) take input csv file with "-f" command line option, which in this case would be the @data-carousel-AM/data/prodsyslogs.csv file
2) scan the "-f" input csv file, for all rows matching "data_format_short"=="RAW" and "data_origin"=="data", write the rows to a
new data-carousel-AM/data/new-RAW.csv
3) scan the "-f" input csv file, for all rows matching "data_format_short"=="AOD" and "data_origin"=="data", write the rows to a
new data-carousel-AM/data/new-data-AOD.csv
4) scan the "-f" input csv file, for all rows matching "data_format_short"=="AOD" and "data_origin"=="mc", write the rows to a
new data-carousel-AM/data/new-mc-AOD.csv
5) scan the "-f" input csv file, for all rows matching "data_format_short"=="HITS" and "data_origin"=="mc", write the rows to a
new data-carousel-AM/data/new-mc-HITS.csv
6) scan the "-f" input csv file, for all rows already selected by the above 1)~5) steps, drop them, write the remaining rows to
a new data-carousel-AM/data/others.csv
7) for the above 6 new csv files generated from the above 1)~6) steps, split each of them into two, one with "task_type"=="production",
named <original csv filename>-production.csv; another with "task_type"=="analysis", named <original csv filename>-analysis.csv.

Totally 18 new csv files to be generated from the "-f" file. 

--task B: extend the analysis to include the more recent recall history with the new csv format

- the current arcmeta scripts are designed to use the old csv format, refer to the @comm-context
for a comparing table mapping the colume names between the old and new csv files.
- change the arcmeta scripts so that they work for both old and new formats, automatically switch
between the formats based on what's in the specified csv file. For example, if a script is to
count the number of datasets recalled within the same day based on "asctime" column in the old
csv, change the script so that the script will know that "asctime" and "dataset_format_short" are
exchangable so that the script automatically covers the different names across input csv files.

